H5300.definition:
for H5304 (נְפִיסִים);
Nephushesim, a Temple-servant
KJV: Nephisesim (from the margin).

H5301.definition:
a primitive root;
to puff, in various applications (literally, to inflate, blow hard, scatter, kindle, expire; figuratively, to disesteem)
KJV: blow, breath, give up, cause to lose (life), seething, snuff.

H5302.definition:
from H5301 (נָפַח); a gust;
Nophach, a place in Moab
KJV: Nophah.

H5303.definition:
or נְפִל; from H5307 (נָפַל);
properly, a feller, i.e. a bully or tyrant
KJV: giant.

H5304.definition:
plural from an unused root meaning to scatter; expansions;
Nephisim, a Temple-servant
KJV: Nephusim (from the margin).

H5305.definition:
from H5314 (נָפַשׁ); refreshed;
Naphish, a son of Ishmael, and his posterity
KJV: Naphish.

H5306.definition:
from an unused root meaning to glisten;
shining; a gem, probably the garnet
KJV: emerald.

H5307.definition:
a primitive root;
to fall, in a great variety of applications (intransitive or causative, literal or figurative)
KJV: be accepted, cast (down, self, (lots), out), cease, die, divide (by lot), (let) fail, (cause to, let, make, ready to) fall (away, down, -en, -ing), fell(-ing), fugitive, have (inheritance), inferior, be judged (by mistake for H6419 (פָּלַל)), lay (along), (cause to) lie down, light (down), be ([idiom] hast) lost, lying, overthrow, overwhelm, perish, present(-ed, -ing), (make to) rot, slay, smite out, [idiom] surely, throw down.

H5308.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H5307 (נָפַל)
{to fall, in a great variety of applications (intransitive or causative, literal or figurative)}
KJV: fall (down), have occasion.

H5309.definition:
or נֵפֶל; from H5307 (נָפַל);
something fallen, i.e. an abortion
KJV: untimely birth.

H5310.definition:
a primitive root;
to dash to pieces, or scatter
KJV: be beaten in sunder, break (in pieces), broken, dash (in pieces), cause to be discharged, dispersed, be overspread, scatter.

H5311.definition:
from H5310 (נָפַץ);
a storm (as dispersing)
KJV: scattering.

H5312.definition:
(Aramaic) a primitive root;
to issue; causatively, to bring out
KJV: come (go, take) forth (out).

H5313.definition:
(Aramaic) from H5312 (נְפַק);
an outgo, i.e. expense
KJV: expense.

H5314.definition:
a primitive root;
to breathe; passively, to be breathed upon , i.e. (figuratively) refreshed (as if by a current of air)
KJV: (be) refresh selves (-ed).

H5315.definition:
from H5314 (נָפַשׁ);
properly, a breathing creature, i.e. animal of (abstractly) vitality; used very widely in a literal, accommodated or figurative sense (bodily or mental)
KJV: any, appetite, beast, body, breath, creature, [idiom] dead(-ly), desire, [idiom] (dis-) contented, [idiom] fish, ghost, [phrase] greedy, he, heart(-y), (hath, [idiom] jeopardy of) life ([idiom] in jeopardy), lust, man, me, mind, mortally, one, own, person, pleasure, (her-, him-, my-, thy-) self, them (your) -selves, [phrase] slay, soul, [phrase] tablet, they, thing, ([idiom] she) will, [idiom] would have it.

H5316.definition:
for H5299 (נָפָה);
a height
KJV: country.

H5317.definition:
from H5130 (נוּף) in the sense of shaking to pieces;
a dripping i.e. of honey (from the comb)
KJV: honeycomb.

H5318.definition:
from H6605 (פָּתַח); opened, i.e. a spring;
Nephtoach, a place in Palestine
KJV: Neptoah.

H5319.definition:
from H6617 (פָּתַל);
properly, wrestled; but used (in the plural) transitively, a struggle
KJV: wrestling.

H5321.definition:
from H6617 (פָּתַל); my wrestling;
Naphtali, a son of Jacob, with the tribe descended from him, and its territory
KJV: Naphtali.

H5322.definition:
from H5340 (נָצַץ);
a flower (from its brilliancy); also a hawk (from it flashing speed)
KJV: blossom, hawk.

H5323.definition:
a primitive root;
to go away
KJV: flee.

H5324.definition:
a primitive root;
to station, in various applications (literally or figuratively)
KJV: appointed, deputy, erect, establish, [idiom] Huzzah (by mistake for a proper name), lay, officer, pillar, present, rear up, set (over, up), settle, sharpen, establish, (make to) stand(-ing, still, up, upright), best state.

H5325.definition:
passive participle of H5324 (נָצַב);
fixed, i.e. a handle
KJV: haft.

H5326.definition:
(Aramaic) from a root corresponding to H5324 (נָצַב);
fixedness, i.e. firmness
KJV: strength.

H5327.definition:
a primitive root;
properly, to go forth, i.e. (by implication) to be expelled, and (consequently) desolate; causatively, to lay waste; also (specifically), to quarrel
KJV: be laid waste, runinous, strive (together).

H5328.definition:
feminine of H5322 (נֵץ);
a blossom
KJV: flower.

H5330.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H5329 (נָצַח);
to become chief
KJV: be preferred.

H5331.definition:
or נֵצַח; from H5329 (נָצַח);
properly, a goal, i.e. the bright object at adistance travelled towards; hence (figuratively), splendor, or (subjectively) truthfulness, or (objectively) confidence; but usually (adverbially), continually (i.e. to the most distant point of view)
KJV: alway(-s), constantly, end, ([phrase] n-) ever(more), perpetual, strength, victory.

H5332.definition:
probably identical with H5331 (נֶצַח), through the idea of brilliancy of color;
juice of the grape (as blood red)
KJV: blood, strength.

H5333.definition:
or נְצִב; from H5324 (נָצַב);
something stationary, i.e. a prefect, a military post, a statue
KJV: garrison, officer, pillar.

H5334.definition:
the same as H5333 (נְצִיב); station;
Netsib, a place in Palestine
KJV: Nezib.

H5335.definition:
from H5329 (נָצַח); conspicuous;
Netsiach, a Temple-servant
KJV: Neziah.

H5336.definition:
from H5341 (נָצַר);
properly, conservative; but used passively, delivered
KJV: preserved.

H5337.definition:
a primitive root;
to snatch away, whether in a good or a bad sense
KJV: [idiom] at all, defend, deliver (self), escape, [idiom] without fail, part, pluck, preserve, recover, rescue, rid, save, spoil, strip, [idiom] surely, take (out).

H5338.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H5337 (נָצַל);
to extricate
KJV: deliver, rescue.

H5339.definition:
from H5322 (נֵץ);
a blossom
KJV: flower.

H5340.definition:
a primitive root;
to glare, i.e. be bright-colored
KJV: sparkle.

H5341.definition:
a primitive root;
to guard, in a good sense (to protect, maintain, obey, etc.) or a bad one (to conceal, etc.)
KJV: besieged, hidden thing, keep(-er, -ing), monument, observe, preserve(-r), subtil, watcher(-man).

H5342.definition:
from H5341 (נָצַר) in the sense of greenness as a striking color;
a shoot; figuratively, a descendant
KJV: branch.

H5343.definition:
(Aramaic) from a root corresponding to H5352 (נָקָה);
clean
KJV: pure.

H5344.definition:
a primitive root;
to puncture, literally (to perforate, with more or less violence) or figuratively (to specify, designate, libel)
KJV: appoint, blaspheme, bore, curse, express, with holes, name, pierce, strike through.

H5346.definition:
the same as H5345 (נֶקֶב); dell;
Nekeb, a place in Palestine
KJV: Nekeb.

H5347.definition:
from H5344 (נָקַב);
female (from the sexual form)
KJV: female.

H5348.definition:
from an unused root meaning to mark (by puncturing or branding);
spotted
KJV: speckled.

H5349.definition:
active participle from the same as H5348 (נָקֹד);
a spotter (of sheep or cattle), i.e. the owner or tender (who thus marks them)
KJV: herdman, sheepmaster.

H5350.definition:
from the same as H5348 (נָקֹד);
a crumb (as broken to spots); also a biscuit (as pricked)
KJV: cracknel, mouldy.

H5351.definition:
feminine of H5348 (נָקֹד);
a boss
KJV: stud.

H5352.definition:
a primitive root;
to be (or make) clean (literally or figuratively); by implication (in an adverse sense) to be bare, i.e. extirpated
KJV: acquit [idiom] at all, [idiom] altogether, be blameless, cleanse, (be) clear(-ing), cut off, be desolate, be free, be (hold) guiltless, be (hold) innocent, [idiom] by no means, be quit, be (leave) unpunished, [idiom] utterly, [idiom] wholly.

H5353.definition:
feminine of H5348 (נָקֹד) (in the figurative sense of marked); distinction;
Nekoda, a Temple-servant
KJV: Nekoda.

H5354.definition:
a primitive root;
to loathe
KJV: weary.

H5355.definition:
or נָקִיא; (Joel 4:19; Jonah [1:14), from H5352 (נָקָה);
innocent
KJV: blameless, clean, clear, exempted, free, guiltless, innocent, quit.

H5356.definition:
or נִקָּיֹן; from H5352 (נָקָה);
clearness (literally or figuratively)
KJV: cleanness, innocency.

H5357.definition:
from an unused root meaning to bore;
a cleft
KJV: hole.

H5358.definition:
a primitive root;
to grudge, i.e. avenge or punish
KJV: avenge(-r, self), punish, revenge (self), [idiom] surely, take vengeance.

H5359.definition:
from H5358 (נָקַם);
revenge
KJV: [phrase] avenged, quarrel, vengeance.

H5360.definition:
feminine of H5359 (נָקָם);
avengement, whether the act of the passion
KJV: [phrase] avenge, revenge(-ing), vengeance.

H5361.definition:
a primitive root;
to feel aversion
KJV: be alienated.

H5362.definition:
a primitive root;
to strike with more or less violence (beat, fell, corrode); by implication (of attack) to knock together, i.e. surround or circulate
KJV: compass (about, -ing), cut down, destroy, go round (about), inclose, round.

H5363.definition:
from H5362 (נָקַף);
a threshing (of olives)
KJV: shaking.

H5364.definition:
from H5362 (נָקַף);
probably a rope (as encircling)
KJV: rent.

H5365.definition:
a primitive root;
to bore (penetrate, quarry)
KJV: dig, pick out, pierce, put (thrust) out.

H5366.definition:
from H5365 (נָקַר), a fissure
{to bore (penetrate, quarry)}
KJV: cleft, clift.

H5367.definition:
a primitive root;
to entrap (with a noose), literally or figuratively
KJV: catch (lay a) snare.

H5368.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H5367 (נָקַשׁ); used in the sense of H5362 (נָקַף);
to knock
KJV: smote.

H5369.definition:
the same as H5216 (נִיר); lamp;
Ner, an Israelite
KJV: Ner.

H5370.definition:
of foreign origin;
Nergal, a Cuthite deity
KJV: Nergal.

H5371.definition:
from H5370 (נֵרְגַּל) and H8272 (שַׁרְאֶצֶר);
Nergal-Sharetser, the name of two Babylonians
KJV: Nergal-sharezer.

H5372.definition:
from an unused root meaning to roll to pieces;
a slanderer
KJV: talebearer, whisperer.

H5373.definition:
of foreign origin;
nard, an aromatic
KJV: spikenard.

H5374.definition:
or נֵרִיָּהוּ; from H5216 (נִיר) and H3050 (יָהּ); light of Jah;
Nerijah, an Israelite
KJV: Neriah.

H5375.definition:
or נָסָה; (Psalm 4:6 (H7 (אֲבַד))), a primitive root;
to lift, in a great variety of applications, literal and figurative, absolute and relative
KJV: accept, advance, arise, (able to, (armor), suffer to) bear(-er, up), bring (forth), burn, carry (away), cast, contain, desire, ease, exact, exalt (self), extol, fetch, forgive, furnish, further, give, go on, help, high, hold up, honorable ([phrase] man), lade, lay, lift (self) up, lofty, marry, magnify, [idiom] needs, obtain, pardon, raise (up), receive, regard, respect, set (up), spare, stir up, [phrase] swear, take (away, up), [idiom] utterly, wear, yield.

H5376.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H5375 (נָשָׂא)
{to lift}
KJV: carry away, make insurrection, take.

H5377.definition:
a primitive root;
to lead astray, i.e. (mentally) to delude, or (morally) to seduce
KJV: beguile, deceive, [idiom] greatly, [idiom] utterly.

H5378.definition:
a primitive root (perhaps identical with H5377 (נָשָׁא), through the idea of imposition);
to lend on interest; by implication, to dun fordebt
KJV: [idiom] debt, exact, giver of usury.

H5379.definition:
passive participle feminine of H5375 (נָשָׂא);
something taken, i.e. a present
KJV: gift.

H5380.definition:
a primitive root;
to blow; by implication, to disperse
KJV: (cause to) blow, drive away.

H5381.definition:
a primitive root;
to reach (literally or figuratively)
KJV: ability, be able, attain (unto), (be able to, can) get, lay at, put, reach, remove, wax rich, [idiom] surely, (over-) take (hold of, on, upon).

H5382.definition:
a primitive root;
to forget; figuratively, to neglect; causatively, to remit, remove
KJV: forget, deprive, exact.

H5383.definition:
a primitive root (rather identical with H5382 (נָשָׁה), in the sense of H5378 (נָשָׁא));
to lend or (by reciprocity) borrow on security or interest
KJV: creditor, exact, extortioner, lend, usurer, lend on (taker on) usury.

H5384.definition:
from H5382 (נָשָׁה), in the sense of failure;
rheumatic or crippled (from the incident to Jacob)
KJV: which shrank.

H5385.definition:
or rather, נְשֻׂאָה; feminine. passive participle of H5375 (נָשָׂא);
something borne, i.e. a load
KJV: carriage.

H5386.definition:
from H5383 (נָשָׁה);
a debt
KJV: debt.

H5387.definition:
or נָשִׂא; from H5375 (נָשָׂא);
properly, an exalted one, i.e. a king or sheik; also a rising mist
KJV: captain, chief, cloud, governor, prince, ruler, vapour.

H5389.definition:
(Aramaic) irregular plural feminine of H606 (אֱנָשׁ)
{a man}
KJV: women.

H5390.definition:
from H5401 (נָשַׁק);
a kiss
KJV: kiss.

H5391.definition:
a primitive root;
to strike with a sting (as a serpent); figuratively, to oppress with interest on a loan
KJV: bite, lend upon usury.

H5392.definition:
from H5391 (נָשַׁךְ);
interest on a debt
KJV: usury.

H5393.definition:
for H3957 (לִשְׁכָּה);
a cell
KJV: chamber.

H5394.definition:
a primitive root;
to pluck off, i.e. divest, eject or drop
KJV: cast (out), drive, loose, put off (out), slip.

H5395.definition:
a primitive root;
properly, to blow away, i.e. destroy
KJV: destroy.

H5396.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H5397 (נְשָׁמָה);
vital breath
KJV: breath.

H5397.definition:
from H5395 (נָשַׁם);
a puff, i.e. wind, angry or vital breath, divine inspiration, intellect. or (concretely) an animal
KJV: blast, (that) breath(-eth), inspiration, soul, spirit.

H5398.definition:
a primitive root;
to breeze, i.e. blow up fresh (as the wind)
KJV: blow.

H5399.definition:
from H5398 (נָשַׁף);
properly, a breeze, i.e. (by implication) dusk (when the evening breeze prevails)
KJV: dark, dawning of the day (morning), night, twilight.
